2026-10-05: wsfulton
            A typemap for a fixed size array, such as 'int [ANY]', is no longer used for an array
            of unknown size, such as 'int []'. An [ANY] typemap can rely on the array size, such as
            by using $1_dim0, which was empty, so the code generated did not compile. A typemap
            that does not need the size can be copied for the array of unknown size, for example:

