	    [PHP] Adjust generated code to be compatible with PHP 8.6.

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            [OCaml] Fix a heap overflow in the carray.i typemaps for an array parameter, which
            allocated one byte per element instead of the size of an element. In C++, an array
            of a simple type such as int or double, which is allocated with malloc, is now also
            released with free instead of delete [].

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            Fix syntax error for sizeof applied to a member of a parenthesised expression, such as:

              const size_t n = sizeof (x).m;
              void f(size_t n = sizeof (p)->m);

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            #543 Fix syntax error for a pointer, reference or array of pointers type-id used as
            the default of a template type parameter, such as:

              template<class T = int *> struct P {...};
              template<class T1, class T2 = T1 *[2]> struct Q {...};

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            [PHP] Fix a C++11 enum class enumerator initialised by a character literal, which was
            wrapped by code that did not compile, such as:

              enum class Letter { A = 'a', B };

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            Fix a reference to a function used as a parameter or return type, which was wrapped
            by code that did not compile, or crashed SWIG for D, such as:

              typedef int Fn(int);
              int call(int (&f)(int), int i);
              int call_typedef(Fn &f, int i);
              int (&get())(int);
              Fn &get_typedef();

            It is now wrapped in the same way as a pointer to a function, so a function pointer
            constant or the result of get() can be passed to call().

            A function returning a reference to an array, such as 'int (&get_array())[4]', is
            also parsed correctly now. As when the array type is a typedef, it returns a pointer
            to the array instead of a pointer to its first element.

            *** POTENTIAL INCOMPATIBILITY ***

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            A member function declared through a function typedef with an rvalue ref-qualifier
            is now ignored by default with warning 405, the same as when it is written out in
            full, instead of being wrapped by code that does not compile:

              typedef int Fn(int) &&;
              struct S {
                Fn f;
              };

            It can be unignored in the same way too, such as with %feature("ignore", "0") S::f;.
            Warning 405 is also no longer issued for the typedef itself.

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            Fix a possible crash when using -macroerrors, such as when a multiline macro expands
            another macro.

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            Fix the line numbers in warnings and errors for the code following a multiline
            macro expansion when using -macroerrors. They were counted from the last code before
            the macro invocation instead of from the invocation, so any blank lines, comments or
            macro definitions in between were not counted.

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            [Go] Fix Go code that does not compile when wrapping an array that has a '<'
            operator in a dimension, such as:

              int grid[LEN << 1];

            The '<' was mistaken for the start of a template argument list, so the array was
            wrapped as an unknown type and an invalid 'type int interface' was generated.

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            Fix an enum value that is a wide character literal failing with "Type error.
            Expecting an integral type". It is now accepted, the same as a plain character
            literal:

              enum E { A = L'w', B = L'\x263A' };

            Also fix the value of a wide character literal holding a character that is not
            ASCII, such as L'\x263A' or the character written as itself, used for a constant
            or default argument. It was truncated to a single byte, or split into the bytes of
            its UTF-8 encoding.

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            A wide raw string literal, such as LR"(text)", is now parsed as a wide string literal,
            the same as L"text", instead of as a narrow string literal. The generated code for a
            constant or a C++11 auto variable initialised by one no longer uses a narrow string,
            which did not compile, and a compact default argument no longer passes a narrow string
            where a wide string is expected:

              %constant const wchar_t *C = LR"(text)";
              auto v = LR"(text)";
              %feature("compactdefaultargs") f;
              void f(const wchar_t *s = LR"(text)");

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            [Go] Fix the generated code failing to compile for a constant initialised by a wide
            string literal:

              %constant const wchar_t *C = L"text";

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            Fix a crash wrapping a reference to a function declared through a function typedef:

              typedef int Fn(int);
              Fn &fnref = fn;

            The reference is now wrapped as a function, the same as a reference to a function
            declared without a typedef. A member function declared through a const qualified
            function typedef is also fixed, as its wrapper did not compile:

              typedef int CFn(int) const;
              struct S {
                CFn f;
              };

2026-10-01: wsfulton
            [Javascript] Fix a member function declared through a function typedef, which was
